@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@*
    #251 · THE NEAREST-BODY, RADAR, PLASMA AND PULSE LINES, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of NavHud.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that
    was in the HUD, character for character. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME
    (fields keep their underscore, methods come across as delegates under their own names), which is what
    lets the markup move without a rewrite and lets MapMarkup splice it straight back where it came from.

    IHandleEvent repeats NavHud's own override, which repeats Map.Sim.cs's: the HUD's refresh belongs to
    OnTick's 200 ms throttle, and a child that did not repeat it would put an automatic render back on
    every event in here. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules; it exists to give the component
    Map.razor.css's scope (pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every rule that styled these elements
    goes on matching them.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block came out of a Razor CODE block, and
    a code block is where its first statements are legal. It is outside the fences, so what the source
    guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the HUD.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from NavHud.razor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
            <div>
                @* #954: one line for a fact that needs two — the neighbourhood and the thing in it, and the
                   ⚓ hint follows the neighbourhood's haven rather than blinking with the nearest slot. *@
                Nearest: @NearestReadoutName() (@FormatDistance((_ship.Position - _nearestBodyPosition).Length), @(((_ship.Velocity - _nearestBodyVelocity).Length / 1000).ToString("F1", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) km/s rel)@if (_nearestHaven is not null && _dockedHavenId is null)
                {
                    <span class="text-info"> · ⚓ dockable haven — coast within @((DockReachMeters / 1000).ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) km, ≤@((DockMatchSpeedMps / 1000).ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) km/s to clamp on</span>
                }
            </div>
            @if (_activeRadar)
            {
                <div class="text-danger">📡 ACTIVE RADAR — loud; everyone in earshot knows where we are</div>
            }
            @if (_plasma is not null)
            {
                int chargePct = (int)Math.Round(_ship.Charge * 100);
                string chargeClass = _ship.Charge >= ArcChargeThreshold ? "bg-danger"
                    : _ship.Charge >= 0.6 ? "bg-warning" : "bg-info";
                <hr />
                <div>Charge: @chargePct% @(_ship.Charge >= ArcChargeThreshold ? "— ARCING RISK" : "")</div>
                <div class="progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Hull charge">
                    <div class="progress-bar @chargeClass" style="width: @chargePct%"></div>
                </div>
                @if (_ship.Charge >= ArcChargeThreshold)
                {
                    <div class="text-danger fw-bold">⚡ ARCING — visible system-wide</div>
                }
            }
            @if (_pulse.Message is not null)
            {
                <div class="text-warning">@_pulse.Message</div>
            }
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
